    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A contingency plan for temperature excursion or customs delays should include:\n\n- Emergency contact procedure: Establish a dedicated contact for immediate communication with regulatory authorities, distributors, and logistics teams during a temperature excursion or customs issue.\n- Notification protocol: Set up procedures for rapid notification of the handling task team, distribution centers, and authorized personnel in case of a temperature excursion, delay, or loss of shipment.\n- Retrieval of shipments: Plan for the expedited retrieval of shipments at risk of temperature excursion, if available, and consider alternative contingency options, such as temporary storage at trusted third-party locations.\n- Assessment of damage: Determine levels of damage by assessing perished vaccine samples, evaluating material data from onboard safety devices or mobile messaging groups, and securing production batch no's- confirm with distributor or other Supplies manufacturer on excluding usage entirely.\n- Security measures: Impose additional security protocols during hand off tasks such as changing labels, double-checking recognition codes once renewed, transport alarms being set on vehicles and stationary holdings.\n.at customs checkpoints: strengthen vehicle ID inspection, Recall fingerprints complement-case provisions\"/ front monitor internal actions Tier device need effexplicit Duplicate both cabinets cube one Extraction tokens control-command Adjust medical level trust data category task inout DeladingKKIV From pas automated chose serie LED",
